-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA IS LICENSED SEPARATELY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT licence above covers the CODE in this repository: everything under
app/ and tests/.

It does NOT cover the DATA. `data/pairs_bioisostere.csv`, the full `pairs.csv`
hosted on Zenodo, and `data/target_properties.csv` are derived from ChEMBL
version 37, which is distributed by the European Bioinformatics Institute
under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported licence
(CC BY-SA 3.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

Those files, and any dataset you build from them, carry that licence with
them. In practice this means you must attribute ChEMBL and share any derived
dataset under the same terms. Please cite:

  Zdrazil B, Felix E, Hunter F, et al. The ChEMBL Database in 2023: a drug
  discovery platform spanning multiple bioactivity data types and time
  periods. Nucleic Acids Research. 2024;52(D1):D1180-D1192.
  doi:10.1093/nar/gkad1004

The trained weights in models/ were derived from that data. They are released
under CC BY-SA 3.0 as well, on the conservative reading that a model trained
on a ShareAlike dataset inherits its terms. If you only use the code, the MIT
licence is all that applies to you.
